From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:33:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: cs_dsp: don't treat a changed control as a write
 sequence error

cs_dsp_coeff_write_ctrl() returns 1 when the control's value changed. The
write sequence code checked "if (ret)", so the first write of any new
entry failed with 1 and cs_dsp_wseq_write() returned it to the caller.
Only negative values are errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/firmware/cirrus/cs_dsp.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/cirrus/cs_dsp.c b/drivers/firmware/cirrus/cs_dsp.c
index bb93b24c6..ac868b0ec 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/cirrus/cs_dsp.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/cirrus/cs_dsp.c
@@ -3780,7 +3780,7 @@ int cs_dsp_wseq_write(struct cs_dsp *dsp, struct cs_dsp_wseq *wseq,
 
 		ret = cs_dsp_coeff_write_ctrl(wseq->ctl, op_end->offset / sizeof(u32),
 					      &op_end->data, sizeof(u32));
-		if (ret)
+		if (ret < 0)
 			goto op_new_free;
 
 		list_add_tail(&op_new->list, &op_end->list);
@@ -3788,7 +3788,7 @@ int cs_dsp_wseq_write(struct cs_dsp *dsp, struct cs_dsp_wseq *wseq,
 
 	ret = cs_dsp_coeff_write_ctrl(wseq->ctl, op_new->offset / sizeof(u32),
 				      words, new_op_size);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret < 0)
 		goto op_new_free;
 
 	return 0;
